{"text": "\u00a5\n\nLeta,\n\ninbiialitoeiaddl 1, Retiaiiinbieed .. Meneame\n\naed a\n\nee\n\nCURTIS 4. JUDGE\n\nApril 2, 1982\n\nThe Honorable Stewart B. McKinney\nHouse of Representatives\nWashington, D. C. 20025\n\nRe: H.R. 5653 - Waxmap Bill\n\nDear Congressman McKinney:\n\nIn my opinion, the Waxman Bill, under\nthe guise of informing the public about the\nhealth consequences of smoking, would impose\nsevere new curbs on cigarette labeling and\nadvertising and lay the foundation for a re-\naewed campaign of harassment of the tobacco\nindustry.\n\nIn these days when the Administration an\u00e9\nmost elected officials are seeking less bureau-\ncratic intervention into business and private\n\nlives, this bill seems to be swimming against\nthe current.\n\nAs one of your constituents, I earnestly\n\nurge you to oppose this ill-conceived legisla-\ntion.\n\nTEEstT9aLo",
